cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "The Epstein Files Collection — archive index of official releases, mirrors, torrents and checksums"
message: "If you use this index in research, please cite it using the DOI below."
type: dataset
authors:
  - name: "The Epstein Files Collection contributors"
    website: "https://github.com/nukIeer/epstein-files"
abstract: >-
  A pointer-only index of publicly released Epstein Files Transparency Act (EFTA)
  materials and related DOJ, House Oversight and court productions. The index records
  magnet URIs, BitTorrent infohashes, official and mirror URLs, and published SHA-256
  checksums for each release. It contains no document blobs: it is a few hundred
  kilobytes of metadata describing terabytes of material held on the Internet Archive,
  in BitTorrent swarms, and on justice.gov. Rebuilt daily from a curated source list,
  and shipped with tooling to verify a downloaded artifact against the recorded
  checksums.
keywords:
  - Epstein Files
  - EFTA
  - H.R.4405
  - DOJ
  - public records
  - FOIA
  - digital preservation
  - BitTorrent
  - data archiving
  - provenance
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22865745"
license: CC0-1.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/nukIeer/epstein-files"
version: "0.3.0"
date-released: "2026-09-20"
references:
  - type: legislation
    title: "Epstein Files Transparency Act of 2025 (H.R.4405)"
    url: "https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/4405"
  - type: database
    title: "U.S. Department of Justice — Epstein files release"
